[
  {
    "language_code": "",
    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "And the West had done this before. During the Cold War, America and its allies ran a committee called CoCom, which blocked sales of advanced technology to the Soviet Union. The Soviets answered with an entire spy operation, known as Line X, dedicated to stealing or smuggling Western technology. Its most famous win came to light in nineteen eighty seven. A subsidiary of Japan's Toshiba and Norway's Kongsberg had sold the Soviets precision milling machines that helped make their submarines much harder to hear. Americans were furious. Members of Congress smashed a Toshiba radio with sledgehammers on the Capitol lawn. Forty years later, the same game is back. Only now, the prize fits on your fingertip.",
